@page "/"
@page "/index.html"
@inject IJSRuntime JsRuntime

<PageTitle>TiltanTale</PageTitle>

@*
    The canvas is the whole game. It's sized by CSS to fill the page and
    letterboxed with object-fit, so the 3:2 picture keeps its shape at any
    window size — the browser's answer to GameSettings.FitToScreen.

    image-rendering:pixelated matters here: the art is 20px tiles and an 8px
    font, and the default smooth upscale turns both to mush. It's the CSS
    equivalent of the SamplerState.PointClamp every Begin() in the game uses.
*@
<div id="canvasHolder">
    <canvas id="theCanvas"></canvas>
</div>

<style>
    html, body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #000;
    }

    #canvasHolder {
        position: fixed;
        inset: 0;
        background: #000;
    }

    #theCanvas {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: contain;
        image-rendering: pixelated;
        image-rendering: crisp-edges;
        touch-action: none;
    }
</style>
